As long as you're fast and unburdened, D and J double teaming you with
extreme bad luck and really wonky circumstances always leaves you with
at least 2 turns to act.  Really unless something bizarre (involving
Juiblex engulfing you and then getting killed by forces beyond your
control) happens it'll be at least 3 turns (and hence at least 4 moves
since you're fast).

I suppose if you're a ranger who lures Scorpius, D, and J to Astral
adjacent to Pestilence then there's a scenario where not being very
fast could leave you unable to go into the bag for a cure.  I generally
use blessed !speed just before leaving Water, but I didn't have that
case in mind.

Anyway, sickness is quite uncommon.  Situations where jumping can save
you are much more common in my experience.

>  By the time you hit Astral, the riders
> aren't that bad so long as you are prepared for them.  Jumping on
> Astral is an interesting strategy, though, that I have yet to try.

You'll like it.  When you do it, bear in mind that you can jump
diagonally into/out of/through doors (even though you can't walk
diagonally in/out of them).  And you can generally avoid bothering with
the riders, just jump past them and /teleport to make jumping lanes
(don't teleport the Riders, teleport everything else).  Learning to go
diagonally to weave through traffic is key.

Just remember to bring light.  I've been known to wish up a blessed oil
lamp on Astral a couple of times.



